From cd8e3c77ce42cdd7598266879eccd845f2942b4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add the SS3-matched Indian Ocean yellowfin article

New article io-yft-ss3-matched takes the age-based fit A-SS3 (AGE here)
closer to the SS3 configuration: SS3's lambda of 0 on parameter priors
(AGE-NP), and SS3's generalised size compositions for the index on their
own bins with SS3's lambda of 0.51 (AGE-NP-SF); AGE-SF keeps the priors.
Without priors the selectivity parameters the data do not inform are held
at their free estimates. The article also records the start sensitivity:
from SS3's solution the no-prior fits stop at a worse optimum with a
stock size close to SS3's.

io_yft_reference$ss3 gains sizefreq and lambdas (exported by
06-export-io-yft-sizefreq-for-opal.r in wcpfc-bet-single-region).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DnfY2GLFTeXdrpNCmFdVQD
